WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar reminding you to Mind Your Decisions.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:12.500
In triangle ABC, angle A is bisected into two equal angles of 60°.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:21.820
If AD = 100, AB = 2(AC), then what it the length of BC?

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.200
This was asked in a math contest in Switzerland and no calculators were allowed.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.740
Pause the video if you like to give it a try,

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:35.700
and when you are ready, keep watching to learn how to solve this problem.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.760
So let's get started solving this problem.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:56.220
If AC has a length of x, then AB = 2x.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:01.440
Now we are going to prove that BD = 2 (DC).

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.700
This follows immediately by the angle bisector theorem,

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.680
but if you didn't remember the angle bisector theorem, let's prove it.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:14.000
So let's get started by labeling ∠ADC as α.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.165
Then ∠ADB would be suplementary,

00:01:17.165 --> 00:01:20.100
so it would be 180° - α.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.040
Next, we'll use the laws of sines,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.220
which I read was first described by the Persian mathematician Tusi.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.920
So let's use the laws of sines in △ADC.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:39.260
This gives that DC / sin 60° = x /sin α.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.800
Next we'll use the laws of sines in △ADB.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:53.100
This gives that BD / sin 60° = 2x /sin (180° - α).

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:59.460
Next ,we use the identity that the sine of an angle is the same as its supplementary angle,

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.200
so we can simplify this fraction.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:07.040
Now, let's multiply both equations by sin 60°,

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:11.900
and then we divide the first equation from the second equation.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.120
We get the ratio BD / DC

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.600
We can now cancel out many terms,

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.060
we'll left with just the fraction equals to 2,

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.880
and this would directly leave to the identity that we want,

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.700
BD = 2 (DC).

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:32.555
So if DC has a length of y,

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.900
BD would have a length of 2y.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.740
Now recall that the length of AD is 100.

00:02:39.395 --> 00:02:42.195
Now we are going to use Al-Kashi's theorem.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:50.960
y² = x² + 100² - 2 (x)(100) cos 60°

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:55.520
Since cos 60° = 1/2, we'll simplify this.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.520
We'll put this equation to aside.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:01.500
And now we'll use Al-Kashi's theorem on this triangle.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.920
We again simplify cos 60° and we get this equation.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.020
So we now have two equations.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:12.760
Let's cancel out the y² terms,

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.560
we'll multiply the first equation by 4,

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.840
and then we would subtract the second equation.

00:03:18.355 --> 00:03:21.545
We cancel terms between the equations

00:03:21.545 --> 00:03:26.200
and left with 0 = 3(100²) - 200x,

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.440
we can then solve that x = 150.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.920
We then go back to the diagram,

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:36.260
and then we are going to use the law of cosines, or Al-Kashi's theorem,

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.220
and we're going to substitute in for x.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:42.740
We get that y² = 17500,

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.360
and then that means y, we wants to take the positive value because we're dealing with a length,

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.460
y would be equal to 50 times the square root of 7.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.660
Now recall we want to solve for BC,

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:58.460
and BC = 3y, so we get 150 times the square root of 7,

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.300
and that's our answer.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.520
This is a great trigonometry problem

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:06.400
you really have to use a lot of concepts

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.005
to work out the final answer,

00:04:09.005 --> 00:04:11.265
and you can do it all without a calculator.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.920
Thanks for watching and for making Mind Your Deicions one of the best YouTube channels.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.300
Thanks for watching and thanks for your support.

